At max-width 820, menu-footer static, so it should be after menu content, not top. But the "OMGITHUB // ARCADE DIVISION" text at top right might be from the 3D scene? Wait the world has side banners "VEXA" and "VOLT RALLY", not OMGITHUB. The text is definitely menu footer. Why top? Look at screenshot: at top right around y=57, "OMGITHUB // ARCADE DIVISION" in two lines. Could be because `.menu-footer` static but inside `.menu` flex container with `justify-content:flex-start; align-items:flex-start;` and it's the third child; flex direction default row! The `.menu` is a flex container (overlay display flex) and at max820 sets `justify-content:flex-start; align-items:flex-start;` but doesn't set `flex-direction: column`. So its children (menu-inner, menu-footer, maybe beams absolute) are laid out in a row! The menu-inner takes width 100%, and menu-footer is pushed to the right of it, off to the side, but because menu-inner width 100% + footer, it may appear at top right due to `align-items:flex-start`. On mobile earlier (390x844), the footer was not visible because it was off-screen to the right (menu scrollWidth 555). That explains the horizontal overflow and 555 width! The beams only accounted partially; the footer adds width.

This is a real responsive layout bug. `.menu` at max-width 820 must be `flex-direction: column;` and `align-items: stretch` perhaps. Then the footer will sit below the content (or hidden). The menu-inner width 100%, footer below. This also may increase scrollHeight but PLAY remains visible. The footer at bottom would add 22px; scrollHeight 685+~30=715, still okay. But fixed horizontal overflow disappears.

On desktop, `.menu` is also row but `.menu-inner` width 54vw and footer absolute, so no issue. At max820, footer static means it participates in flex row. Fix:
```
@media (max-width: 820px) {
 .menu { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
 .menu-footer { ... }
}
```
But `.menu` currently has `align-items:flex-start` in that media. Replace with `flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start;` and footer width 100%. As a flex item in column, footer will be after menu-inner, align-items flex-start means its width auto (based on content), so justify-between doesn't span. Set `.menu-footer { width: 100%; }` or `align-self:stretch`. Add `align-self: stretch;`.
Alternatively set footer `display:none` on mobile (only arcade division/credit, not essential). That simplifies and removes overflow. On mobile, we don't need footer. But maybe keep credit. The menu-footer has two spans, sound hidden. We can hide it at max820 or set proper column. Better set column and keep.

Also the `.menu` eyebrow wrapping at 320: "SUPERPOWERED SPORT // NEO-TOKYO 2088" wraps to 3 lines, which pushes content down; PLAY still visible. Could reduce font size or hide on small screens. At 320, the eyebrow at top overlaps the 3D hologram text. Not a functional issue, but visually messy. We can make it smaller and nowrap with ellipsis? Or hide the "// NEO-TOKYO 2088" part on <=480. Use `.eyebrow` font-size 8px and `white-space: nowrap` with overflow hidden? At 320, the full string ~310px maybe fits at 8px. Let's set at max480 `.eyebrow { font-size: 7.5px; letter-spacing: 0.2em; gap: 6px; }`. It might fit on one line ~270px. Good.

Also at 320, the logo "VOLT" and "RALLY" fit. Good.

The feature row at 320 is one line with tiny 7px labels. Good.

The control cards at 320: card text fits, but the "MOVE" card's description wraps to 2 lines; fine.

Fix menu flex-direction and footer.

Let's patch:
```
@media (max-width: 820px) {
 .menu { justify-content:flex-start; align-items:flex-start; flex-direction: column; ...}
 .menu-footer { position: static; align-self: stretch; margin-top: 22px; ...}
```
`align-items: flex-start` in column means menu-inner width 100% (set), footer align-self stretch. Good.
Also `overflow-x:hidden` still set.
At max480 eyebrow adjust.
At max-height620 landscape `.menu { align-items:center; }` in column -> horizontally centers children but menu-inner width 58vw, footer hidden. Fine.

Add `touch-action: pan-y` to `.menu`.
At 320, the footer below might show "OMGITHUB // ARCADE DIVISION" at bottom; fine.

